  <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
  <p>This application ("the App") connects to your eBay seller account, with your
  explicit consent via eBay's "Sign in with eBay" flow, to automatically end
  low-traffic listings and create replacement listings on your behalf.</p>

  <h2>What we access</h2>
  <p>Once you connect your eBay account, the App can read and modify your eBay
  <strong>listing data</strong> on your behalf:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Your eBay username</li>
    <li>Your active and ended listings: title, description, category, price,
    quantity, item specifics, photos, shipping and return policy settings, and
    view counts</li>
    <li>Ending an active listing, and creating a new listing pre-filled from an
    ended one's details ("sell similar")</li>
  </ul>
  <p>The App does <strong>not</strong> request access to your buyer activity,
  orders, messages, or any payment/financial information — it only reads and
  writes your own listing data.</p>

  <h2>What we store</h2>
  <p>We store, in our own database:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Your eBay username</li>
    <li>Your eBay OAuth refresh token, encrypted at rest (AES-256-GCM) — used to
    act on your behalf between visits, without asking you to sign in every time</li>
    <li>The automation settings you configure: item limit, brand keywords, view
    count and days-left thresholds</li>
    <li>A log of each automation run: which listings were ended/relisted,
    timestamps, and any errors</li>
  </ul>
  <p>We do not store your buyer/order/payment information — we never request
  access to it in the first place.</p>

  <h2>Data retention and deletion</h2>
  <p>We retain the data above for as long as your eBay account stays connected
  to the App. If you delete or close your eBay account, eBay automatically
  notifies us and we permanently delete everything listed above (encrypted
  token, settings, run history).</p>
